  "implementation": [
    "ApplicationRecord exposes a round-scoped signing panel; authorized frozen attachment metadata is read with at most four concurrent requests and no default document or profile selection.",
    "Explicit review and acknowledgement bind documents, profile text version, application source version, purpose and first-send deadline; changed intent or expired confirmation cannot dispatch.",
    "Unsent cancellation binds the original operation and text version; pending writes reuse the existing actor-scoped recovery queue with the original body and idempotency key.",
    "Successful write receipts are validated before pending state is cleared; a bounded write timeout or malformed response retains the original request even if a success later arrives.",
    "History accepts permission-filtered empty pages with a cursor; repeated cursors and inconsistent responses are rejected. Read generations and abort signals prevent late data crossing identities.",
    "Original and signed-result downloads remain separate. Collecting states offer no result download, incomplete bodies are rejected, and object URLs are released.",
    "The parent record keeps header, footer, history and related navigation consistent with pending signing edits and writes. Only the last original operation position is remembered in memory."
  ],
